---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Layout 
  title="Terms of Service - Samford IT Solutions" 
  description="Terms of Service for Samford IT Solutions. Read our terms and conditions for using our services."
>
  <Header />
  
  <main>
    <!-- Hero Section -->
    <section class="relative text-white py-20 thegreen">
      <div class="container-custom">
        <div class="max-w-4xl">
          <h1 class="mb-6 text-5xl economica-bold">Terms of Service</h1>
          <p class="text-xl text-primary-100 leading-relaxed">
            Last Updated: January 22, 2026
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Terms Content -->
    <section class="section bg-white">
      <div class="container-custom max-w-4xl">
        <div class="prose prose-lg max-w-none">
          
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Agreement to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms of Service ("Terms") constitute a legally binding agreement between you (either an individual or entity, "you" or "Client") and Samford IT Solutions ("Company," "we," "us," or "our") governing your use of our website and services.
          </p>
          <p>
            By accessing our website or engaging our services, you agree to be bound by these Terms. If you do not agree to these Terms, you may not access our website or use our services.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Services</h2>
          <p>Samford IT Solutions provides IT solutions and services including but not limited to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Network Cabling</li>
            <li>Data Centre Solutions</li>
            <li>CCTV & Access Control</li>
            <li>Cloud Solutions</li>
            <li>Cybersecurity Services</li>
            <li>Managed IT Support</li>
            <li>Audio Visual Solutions</li>
            <li>UPS Systems</li>
            <li>Biometric Systems and Network Access Control</li>
            <li>IT Relocation Services</li>
            <li>WiFi Optimization</li>
            <li>Fixed Wireless Solutions</li>
            <li>Smart Home Integration</li>
            <li>VOIP Phone Systems</li>
            <li>Other IT infrastructure and support services</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            The specific scope, deliverables, timeline, and pricing for services will be detailed in individual service agreements, statements of work, or quotations.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Service Agreements and Quotations</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Quotations</h3>
          <p>
            All quotations provided are valid for 30 days from the date of issue unless otherwise specified. Quotations are subject to change based on scope modifications, material costs, or other factors beyond our control.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Acceptance</h3>
          <p>
            Services commence upon your acceptance of a quotation or execution of a service agreement. Acceptance may be indicated by signed agreement, purchase order, written confirmation, or payment of deposit.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Scope of Work</h3>
          <p>
            The scope of work will be clearly defined in the service agreement or quotation. Any work outside the agreed scope will be considered additional work and may incur extra charges.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Pricing and Payment</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Fees</h3>
          <p>
            You agree to pay all fees as specified in the applicable quotation or service agreement. All prices are quoted in ZAR (South African Rand) and exclude applicable taxes unless otherwise stated.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Payment Terms</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Payment terms are Net 30 days from invoice date unless otherwise agreed in writing</li>
            <li>A deposit may be required before commencement of work</li>
            <li>We reserve the right to suspend services for accounts with overdue payments</li>
            <li>Late payments may incur interest charges at the maximum rate permitted by law</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Taxes</h3>
          <p>
            You are responsible for all applicable sales, use, value-added, and other taxes associated with the services, excluding taxes based on our net income.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Payment Disputes</h3>
          <p>
            Any payment disputes must be raised within 15 days of invoice date. Undisputed portions of invoices remain due and payable.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Client Responsibilities</h2>
          <p>You agree to:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Provide accurate and complete information necessary for service delivery</li>
            <li>Grant access to premises, systems, and equipment as required</li>
            <li>Ensure a safe working environment for our personnel</li>
            <li>Provide timely feedback and approvals as requested</li>
            <li>Maintain backup copies of all data before any system modifications</li>
            <li>Comply with all applicable laws and regulations</li>
            <li>Notify us promptly of any issues or concerns regarding services</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Intellectual Property</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Our Property</h3>
          <p>
            All intellectual property rights in our services, methodologies, documentation, software, and materials remain our exclusive property or that of our licensors.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Client Property</h3>
          <p>
            You retain all rights to your data, content, and pre-existing intellectual property. By engaging our services, you grant us a limited license to use such materials solely for the purpose of delivering services.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Work Product</h3>
          <p>
            Upon full payment, you will own the specific deliverables created exclusively for you under the service agreement. We retain rights to any pre-existing materials, methodologies, and general knowledge.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Warranties and Disclaimers</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Limited Warranty</h3>
          <p>
            We warrant that services will be performed in a professional and workmanlike manner consistent with industry standards. Equipment and materials supplied will conform to manufacturer specifications.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Warranty Period</h3>
          <p>
            Hardware installations are warranted for 90 days from completion. Software and configuration services are warranted for 30 days from acceptance.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Warranty Exclusions</h3>
          <p>Our warranty does not cover:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Damage caused by misuse, abuse, or negligence</li>
            <li>Unauthorized modifications or repairs</li>
            <li>Normal wear and tear</li>
            <li>Force majeure events</li>
            <li>Third-party products (which are covered by manufacturer warranties)</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Disclaimer</h3>
          <p class="font-semibold">
            EXCEPT AS EXPRESSLY PROVIDED, SERVICES AND MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS" WITHOUT WARRANTIES OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR IMPLIED, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Limitation of Liability</h2>
          <p class="font-semibold">TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY LAW:</p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Liability Cap</h3>
          <p>
            Our total liability for any claims arising from or related to services shall not exceed the total amount paid by you for the specific services giving rise to the claim during the twelve (12) months preceding the claim.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Excluded Damages</h3>
          <p class="font-semibold">
            WE SHALL NOT BE LIABLE FOR ANY INDIRECT, INCIDENTAL, SPECIAL, CONSEQUENTIAL, OR PUNITIVE DAMAGES, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO LOSS OF PROFITS, DATA, BUSINESS OPPORTUNITIES, OR GOODWILL, EVEN IF ADVISED OF THE POSSIBILITY OF SUCH DAMAGES.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Exceptions</h3>
          <p>Nothing in these Terms shall limit or exclude liability for:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Death or personal injury caused by negligence</li>
            <li>Fraud or fraudulent misrepresentation</li>
            <li>Any liability that cannot be limited or excluded by applicable law</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Confidentiality</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Mutual Obligations</h3>
          <p>
            Both parties agree to maintain the confidentiality of any proprietary or confidential information disclosed during the course of the engagement and not to disclose such information to third parties without prior written consent.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Exceptions</h3>
          <p>Confidential information does not include information that:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Is or becomes publicly available through no breach of this agreement</li>
            <li>Was rightfully known prior to disclosure</li>
            <li>Is independently developed without use of confidential information</li>
            <li>Is required to be disclosed by law or court order</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Data Protection and Privacy</h2>
          <p>
            We will process personal data in accordance with our Privacy Policy and applicable data protection laws. You represent and warrant that you have obtained all necessary consents for us to process personal data on your behalf.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Term and Termination</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Term</h3>
          <p>
            These Terms remain in effect for the duration of our service relationship and any ongoing service agreements.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Termination for Convenience</h3>
          <p>
            Either party may terminate ongoing service agreements with 30 days written notice, subject to the terms of specific service agreements.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Termination for Cause</h3>
          <p>Either party may terminate immediately if the other party:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Materially breaches these Terms and fails to cure within 15 days of written notice</li>
            <li>Becomes insolvent or subject to bankruptcy proceedings</li>
            <li>Engages in fraudulent or illegal conduct</li>
          </ul>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Effect of Termination</h3>
          <p>Upon termination:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>You must pay for all services rendered and expenses incurred through the termination date</li>
            <li>We will return or destroy your confidential information as directed</li>
            <li>Provisions that by their nature should survive will remain in effect</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Indemnification</h2>
          <p>
            You agree to indemnify, defend, and hold harmless Samford IT Solutions, its officers, directors, employees, and agents from any claims, damages, losses, liabilities, and expenses (including reasonable legal fees) arising from:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li>Your breach of these Terms</li>
            <li>Your violation of any law or regulation</li>
            <li>Your violation of any third-party rights</li>
            <li>Your negligence or willful misconduct</li>
          </ul>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Force Majeure</h2>
          <p>
            Neither party shall be liable for any failure or delay in performance due to circumstances beyond their reasonable control, including but not limited to acts of God, natural disasters, war, terrorism, labor disputes, government actions, or telecommunications failures.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Modifications to Terms</h2>
          <p>
            We reserve the right to modify these Terms at any time. We will notify you of material changes by posting the updated Terms on our website and updating the "Last Updated" date. Your continued use of our services after such modifications constitutes acceptance of the updated Terms.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Independent Contractor</h2>
          <p>
            Our relationship is that of independent contractors. Nothing in these Terms creates a partnership, joint venture, agency, or employment relationship between the parties.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Third-Party Products and Services</h2>
          <p>
            We may recommend or integrate third-party products and services. We are not responsible for the performance, warranties, or support of third-party products, which are governed by the respective third-party terms and conditions.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Assignment</h2>
          <p>
            You may not assign or transfer these Terms or any rights hereunder without our prior written consent. We may assign these Terms or delegate our obligations without restriction.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Severability</h2>
          <p>
            If any provision of these Terms is found to be invalid or unenforceable, the remaining provisions will remain in full force and effect, and the invalid provision will be modified to the minimum extent necessary to make it valid and enforceable.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Waiver</h2>
          <p>
            Our failure to enforce any right or provision of these Terms will not be deemed a waiver of such right or provision. Any waiver must be in writing and signed by an authorized representative.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Entire Agreement</h2>
          <p>
            These Terms, together with any service agreements, quotations, and our Privacy Policy, constitute the entire agreement between you and Samford IT Solutions regarding the services and supersede all prior agreements and understandings.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Governing Law and Dispute Resolution</h2>
          
          <h3 class="economica-bold">Governing Law</h3>
          <p>
            These Terms shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of South Africa, without regard to its conflict of law provisions.
          </p>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Dispute Resolution</h3>
          <p>Any disputes arising from these Terms or our services shall be resolved through:</p>
          <ol>
            <li>Good faith negotiations between the parties</li>
            <li>Mediation, if negotiations fail</li>
            <li>Binding arbitration or litigation in the courts of South Africa</li>
          </ol>

          <h3 class="economica-bold">Legal Fees</h3>
          <p>
            In any legal proceeding to enforce these Terms, the prevailing party shall be entitled to recover reasonable legal fees and costs.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Notices</h2>
          <p>All notices under these Terms must be in writing and delivered to:</p>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary-600 my-6">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">Samford IT Solutions</p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:infoit@samford.co.za" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">infoit@samford.co.za</a></p>            
            <p>Address: Cape Town, South Africa</p>
          </div>
          <p>
            Notices to you will be sent to the contact information provided in your service agreement or account.
          </p>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Contact Information</h2>
          <p>For questions about these Terms, please contact us at:</p>
          <div class="bg-gray-50 p-6 rounded-lg border-l-4 border-primary-600 my-6">
            <p class="font-semibold mb-2">Samford IT Solutions</p>
            <p>Email: <a href="mailto:infoit@samford.co.za" class="text-primary-600 hover:text-primary-700">infoit@samford.co.za</a></p>            
            <p>Address: Cape Town, South Africa</p>
          </div>

          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl economica-bold">Acceptance</h2>
          <p class="font-semibold text-lg">
            BY USING OUR WEBSITE OR SERVICES, YOU ACKNOWLEDGE THAT YOU HAVE READ, UNDERSTOOD, AND AGREE TO BE BOUND BY THESE TERMS OF SERVICE.
          </p>
          

        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Layout>

<style>
  .prose h2 {
    color: #1e3a8a;
    font-size: 2rem;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 3rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .prose h3 {
    color: #1e3a8a;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .prose p {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: #374151;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  .prose ul,
  .prose ol {
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    margin-left: 1.5rem;
  }

  .prose ul {
    list-style-type: disc;
  }

  .prose ol {
    list-style-type: decimal;
  }

  .prose li {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    color: #374151;
  }

  .prose a {
    color: #3b82f6;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .prose a:hover {
    color: #1e3a8a;
  }
</style>